    "question_type": "mcq",
    "prompt": "A spring-mass system oscillates with period T. If the length of the spring is halved and the mass is reduced to half of its initial mass, what will be the new period?",
    "explanation": "For a spring of stiffness k, T = 2π√(m/k). Halving the natural length doubles the stiffness, and halving the mass gives T' = 2π√((m/2)/(2k)) = T/2.",
